# shadcn/ui Component Library

This project uses **shadcn/ui** for all UI elements. Do not use other component libraries or write raw HTML/CSS components when a shadcn/ui equivalent exists.

## Initialization

If shadcn/ui is not yet initialized in the project, run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Adding Components

If a required component is not installed, add it before using it:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>
```

Examples:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
npx shadcn@latest add input
npx shadcn@latest add dialog
```

## Rules

- Always check `components/ui/` before assuming a component is available.
- Import components from `@/components/ui/<component>`.
- Prefer composing shadcn/ui primitives over building custom alternatives.
- Run the `add` command for any component not yet present in `components/ui/`.
